@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: teach pawn-gas collision with a concrete pair — ally tank versus mecha — using the live collision rule
' status: proposed 2026-09-17, not implemented; _spec/_plans/ is exempt from the SPEC-reference rule.
' would touch: not in this tree — no pawn gas, tank, mecha, or collision types
'   exist under the sandbox checkout (measured 2026-09-17). Locate the owning
'   tutorial module before a covers: line can be honest.
'   the rule this beat teaches ......... _spec/_plans/pawn-first-phase-gas-move.puml
'   the runner it may sit in ........... _spec/_plans/tutorial-interactive-siege.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHAT THE LINE ITEM SETTLES ─────────────────────────────────────────────
' "pawn gas collision (ally tank vs mecha)" is a WORKED EXAMPLE. The pair is
' the fixture: a friendly tank and a mecha share a gas event, and the player
' has to see who is hit. "Ally" is load-bearing — this is friendly fire (or
' the exception to it), not an enemy capture.
'
' ── WHAT IT DOES NOT SETTLE ────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   which of tank or mecha is the ally, and which is the gas source
'   whether mecha is immune, vulnerable, or a different layer
'   damage vs displace vs block
'
' If pawn-first-phase-gas-move.puml changes who occupies the square, this beat
' must be re-shot. Teaching yesterday's collision after the join lands is how
' the tutorial fights the engine.
title PLANNED — ally tank vs mecha is the gas-collision\nfixture; the live rule is the teacher

component "phase-1 pawn gas" as GAS <<app>>
component "ally tank" as TANK <<app>>
component "mecha" as MECH <<app>>
component "live collision rule" as HIT <<app>>
component "tutorial beat\nplayer issues the gas" as BEAT <<app>>
component "**a caption over a film**\nno collision is resolved" as LIE <<error>>

GAS ARROW_MAIN HIT
TANK ARROW_MAIN HIT
MECH ARROW_MAIN HIT
BEAT ARROW_MAIN GAS
HIT ARROW_OPTIONAL LIE : if the beat fakes\nthe result
BEAT ARROW_ERROR LIE

note bottom of HIT
  **The allied tank and mecha pair is the
  collision fixture rather than a generic gas
  demonstration.** They must occupy the tiles the
  collision rule evaluates, or a watch-gas beat
  can pass while this case still fails.
end note

note bottom of BEAT
  **The player must discharge the gas rather than
  watching a scripted collision movie.** The beat
  completes only when their activation intersects
  the named pair under live collision rules.
end note

note right of TANK
  **Ally remains load-bearing, because recasting
  the tank as an enemy produces a different
  collision.** Keep the friendly unit on the board
  so the lesson matches the backlog pair.
end note

legend bottom
  **The order to do it in**
  ==
  **1. Wait on the join, or pin today's rule.** If first-phase gas+occupy is
  about to land, shoot this beat against that build. If not, pin the current
  collision and re-record when the join ships.
  --
  **2. Script the fixture, not the result.** Place ally tank and mecha, unlock
  gas, assert who is hit / not hit / displaced from the engine, not from a
  hard-coded caption.
  ==
  **3. Fail the beat if the player skips the pair.** A win path that never
  vents at the tank does not complete this item.
  --
  **Left open**: who owns the pawn; whether the mecha is ally, enemy, or
  terrain; damage numbers.
end legend
@enduml
